y traffic assertion as an escalation would let any driver freeze any deviation case. The record is decidable, so it is decided. The escalation request is rejected.\n\n4. The money. EV-FARE-00105 shows a METERED fare, so POL-RD-11 does not run and POL-RD-02 fixes the arithmetic. The rider's POL-RD-08 burden is discharged - trip_id TRP-00105 and the 14:33 pickup window match across trip record, trace and fare - and no extra-corroboration filter attaches (rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0). recomputed_fare = 3.80 base + (0.75 x 36.0 = 27.00) distance + (0.28 x 42.0 = 11.76) time + 0.80 platform fee, at surge 1.0 with no ERP, no surcharge and no promo = SGD 43.36. The POL-RD-02 refund is charged_total 65.13 less 43.36 = 21.77, rounded up to SGD 21.80 (above the 0.50 de minimis floor; 33.4% of the charge, below the 90% full-refund share on that limb alone).\n\n5. POL-RD-06 raises that partial to a full refund. A material deviation makes the driver_profile check mandatory, and EV-DPROF-00105 shows deviation_flags_90d of 4, at or above the clause's threshold of 3 - the repeat-deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED. That artifact is IMPAIRED: weight 0.75, issue code STALE_SNAPSHOT (snapshot 2026-07-11T08:00, 108 hours before filing, against a 72-hour threshold), so its counters may lag the driver's state on the trip date and I have not treated the counter as current. The finding survives the discount - 4 against a threshold of 3. Because the deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own evidence, POL-RD-06(b) licenses FULL_REFUND of the charged total in place of the POL-RD-02 partial. Side by side: POL-RD-02 figure SGD 21.80; POL-RD-06(b) uplifted figure SGD 65.13 (a difference of SGD 43.33). No pass-through line is uplifted and none exists: ERP is 0.00, and the 0.00 airport_surcharge line is correct rather than a defect because the Changi surcharge attaches only to trips ORIGINATING at the airport and this trip terminates there. POL-RD-09 therefore adds nothing on top of the refund, and there is no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4).\n\n6. Confidence. The uplift rests on EV-DPROF-00105 at weight 0.75, so under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence is capped at 0.75. That is above the 0.70 platform floor, so no POL-RD-10(1) escalation. The deviation itself is carried by EV-GPS-00105 and EV-TRIP-00105 at weight 1.0.\n\n7. On the discarded material: the rider's claim that POL-RD-03 cannot run, and the rider's framing of the POL-RD-06(c) referral, were both discarded at the mechanical stage for citing impaired artifacts (EV-ADVIS-00105-01; EV-DPROF-00105) without naming their issue codes. The referral in this ruling is not built on either discarded claim: it follows from POL-RD-06(c) itself, which directs a conduct referral once the pattern is established, and the pattern is established on the surviving evidence. The context-only profile fields mentioned on the driver's side (rating, prior_disputes_filed, prior_no_show_flags, prior_deviation_flags, acceptance_rate) were not used as a ground of decision, as POL-GEN-01 requires.\n\nResult: FULL_REFUND of SGD 65.13 to the rider, with the driver referred to conduct review under POL-RD-06(c)."
